            {
              "section": "Epitalon Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "",
              "excerpt": "Mild drowsiness, especially with evening dosing, since the peptide is tied to melatonin signaling.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Epitalon Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "",
              "excerpt": "The bigger safety gaps are about the unknowns, not the known side effects. Long-term human safety data are limited, and the telomerase question matters here too. In theory, switching telomerase on could affect cells you would not want dividing more, which is why people with cancer history are flagged as cautious cases.",
              "truncated": false
            }
          ],
